A||||11||SteveJ||Horses not zebras||||1||
Z||000000||SteveJ||02-22-2001||02:57 PM||||The medical community has a saying, “think horses not zebras." What they mean by that is that when diagnosing a problem first think of the usual problem not the unusual. <P>I see people here in the tech section that really love zebras.<P>So our interest in this concept can be expressed: if it overheats think thermostat and radiator not head gasket; if it shimmies in the front end think wheel balance not bushings or steering gear.<P>Look at the most likely cause of the problem first not the exotic once in a lifetime I saw a case once where. . .<P>Then if that doesn’t do it systematically work through the lesser causes to the least likely ones. <P>Small story:<P>I bought a used ’89 Corsica and the day I picked it up it would not run. It was raining. So I did the wires. No change. Did the plugs. No change. DAMN the effing computer must be getting wet. So I went and bought another at well over $100. In the package came an instruction sheet that said, “Stop you probably don’t need this product! <BR>Go back and recheck your work” and they gave a checklist. There has to be someone really ethical in that company to put this sheet in the box. I followed the checklist by the numbers. But, those f***ing coils hadn’t moved. They were still on the back of the engine right up against the firewall. Hell of a reach from the top. Hell of a reach from the bottom. And yes one of them had a hairline crack and its replacement solved everything.<BR>. . and the parts store refunded the money for the computer because I never cracked the poly bag it was in. <P>Think horses <BR><p>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-22-2001||03:14 PM||||im with you on that, I always try easiest and simplest fix first. My recent experience was a minivan i was thinking of buying. On freeway it ran like crap, shook, jerked and everything u can think of. But started and ran on streets fine, not even a noise or slightest shake. I figured the transmission was bad after changing the spark plugs didnt help. Dealer just replaced a coil pac, and ran perfect so i ended up buying it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||02-22-2001||03:19 PM||||I <I>do</I> think horses. I usually assume, unless obviously otherwise, that whoever asks the question also thinks horses and has already tried all the obvious/easy things.<P>I know that I really hate having to reply "I already thought of that..." twelve dozen times to a question I ask.<P>Unless the person asking comes out and says that he is an automotive simpleton, I don't assume that he is because I don't like it when people assume that about me.<P>Also, whenever I have a question I try to list the obvious solutions that I've unsuccessfully tried.<BR>If everyone did this it would save a lot of confusion and help leave the Zebras in Africa.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||02-22-2001||09:37 PM||||So your troubleshooting tip for the day is <B><I>Check the heads last</B></I>.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
